From 31bd3f3fc858c376325bc028f2ab834fb75c5ebd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 22:39:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] addons: add web apps as an add-on type

A web app is a page shown through Kodi's web view with its own
identity and content. kodi.webapp declares it in addon.xml: a start
URL, one or more user agents by id, user scripts and content filters
as paths in the add-on. The add-on browser lists the type, the info
dialog can run it, and RunAddon opens the start URL through the web
player with the add-on's id as the page's profile, or switches to the
web window when the player already shows that profile, so returning
to a running web app keeps its page.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
